# `optim::SeptimaConstraints`

The constraints of a `septima` run: residual functions for equalities and inequalities, and bounds.

`equalities` returns a vector of residuals `h(x)` that must be zero; `inequalities` returns residuals `g(x)` that must be at most zero; both receive the list of parameter blocks and return a `std::vector<Series>` (one `Series` per group of constraints, scalar or vector). `lbs` and `ubs` are the lower and upper bounds, one `Series` per parameter block in the same order and shape (use `-inf` and `+inf` for no bound). All four are optional. Constraints are enforced by an augmented Lagrangian, so they hold to the tolerance `constraint_tolerance` rather than exactly; bounds are projected. The residual functions must be written with differentiable `Series` operations so that their derivatives are available. Box constraints need an ordering, so bounds are rejected for complex parameters; inequality residuals must be real; equality residuals must be real when `enable_constraint_autodiff` is on.

## Fields

### `equalities`

`std::function<std::vector<pluss::Series>(const std::vector<pluss::Series> &)>`, default `empty`.

Residuals `h(x)` that must be zero.

### `inequalities`

`std::function<std::vector<pluss::Series>(const std::vector<pluss::Series> &)>`, default `empty`.

Residuals `g(x)` that must be at most zero.

### `lbs`

`std::vector<pluss::Series>`, default `empty`.

Lower bounds, one per parameter block.

### `ubs`

`std::vector<pluss::Series>`, default `empty`.

Upper bounds, one per parameter block.

## Guidance

Passed as the fourth argument of `septima`.

## Practical Examples

### Example 1

Bounds. Minimise the distance to `(3, −1)` inside `[0, 2] × [0, 2]`: the nearest corner is `(2, 0)`.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace optim = pluss::subsp::math::optim;
using Pack = optim::ParameterPack<pluss::Series>;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(4));
  const Series target = pluss::series::make({3.0, -1.0});
  optim::SeptimaConstraints constraints;
  constraints.lbs = {pluss::series::make({0.0, 0.0})};
  constraints.ubs = {pluss::series::make({2.0, 2.0})};
  optim::SeptimaSolveOptions options;
  options.step.optimizer = optim::SeptimaOptimizer::Lbfgs;
  const optim::SeptimaResult result = optim::septima([&](const Series &x) { return (x - target).square().sum(); }, pluss::series::make({0.0, 0.0}), options, constraints);
  out.writeln("x =", result.params[0].items<double>());
}
```

### Example 2

An equality, with a vector of residuals. Two equations in one function: `x₀ + x₁ = 2` and `x₀ − x₁ = 0.5`.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace optim = pluss::subsp::math::optim;
using Pack = optim::ParameterPack<pluss::Series>;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(4));
  optim::SeptimaConstraints constraints;
  constraints.equalities = [](const std::vector<Series> &x) {
    return std::vector<Series>{x[0].sum() - 2.0, x[0].select(0, 0) - x[0].select(0, 1) - 0.5};
  };
  optim::SeptimaSolveOptions options;
  options.step.optimizer = optim::SeptimaOptimizer::Lbfgs;
  const optim::SeptimaResult result = optim::septima([](const Series &x) { return x.square().sum(); }, pluss::series::make({0.0, 0.0}), options, constraints);
  out.writeln("x =", result.params[0].items<double>());
  out.writeln("violation =", result.constraint_violation);
}
```

### Example 3

An inequality: `g(x) ≤ 0`. Stay inside the disc `|x|² ≤ 1` while approaching `(1, 2)`.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace optim = pluss::subsp::math::optim;
using Pack = optim::ParameterPack<pluss::Series>;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(4));
  const Series target = pluss::series::make({1.0, 2.0});
  optim::SeptimaConstraints constraints;
  constraints.inequalities = [](const std::vector<Series> &x) { return std::vector<Series>{x[0].square().sum() - 1.0}; };
  optim::SeptimaSolveOptions options;
  options.step.optimizer = optim::SeptimaOptimizer::Lbfgs;
  const optim::SeptimaResult result = optim::septima([&](const Series &x) { return (x - target).square().sum(); }, pluss::series::make({0.0, 0.0}), options, constraints);
  out.writeln("x =", result.params[0].items<double>());
  out.writeln("multiplier =", result.state.lambda_inequalities[0].item<double>());
}
```

### Example 4

Several blocks, with bounds per block. The block order of `lbs` and `ubs` is the order of the initial blocks.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

#include <vector>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace optim = pluss::subsp::math::optim;
using Pack = optim::ParameterPack<pluss::Series>;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(4));
  optim::SeptimaConstraints constraints;
  constraints.lbs = {pluss::series::make({0.5}), pluss::series::make({-10.0})};
  constraints.ubs = {pluss::series::make({10.0}), pluss::series::make({10.0})};
  const std::function<Series(const std::vector<Series> &)> objective = [](const std::vector<Series> &p) { return (p[0] - 0.0).square().sum() + (p[1] - 1.0).square().sum(); };
  optim::SeptimaSolveOptions options;
  options.step.optimizer = optim::SeptimaOptimizer::Lbfgs;
  const optim::SeptimaResult result = optim::septima(objective, std::vector<Series>{pluss::series::make({2.0}), pluss::series::make({2.0})}, options, constraints);
  out.writeln("first =", result.params[0].items<double>(), " second =", result.params[1].items<double>());
}
```

